<title>INDIA: Indian forex reserves fall to $22.36 bln on Aug 16.</title>
<headline>Indian forex reserves fall to $22.36 bln on Aug 16.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves fell to $22.36 billion on August 16, 1996, from $22.41 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>	 FOREIGN EXCHANGE RESERVES (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					   Aug 16	Aug 9	 Aug 18</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     17,887	17,914	 19,004</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,410	 4,410	  4,445</p>
<p>    SDRs				    61	    91	     46</p>
<p>    Total			     22,358	22,415	 23,495</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
